ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE KOREA OCEAN BUSINESS CORPORATION ACT

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Korea Ocean Business Corporation Act and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 1-2 (Scope of shipping and port industries)
"Business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 2, subparagraph 2 (b) of the Korea Ocean Business Corporation Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means ship fuel supply business among port transportation-related businesses under Article 2 (4) of the Port Transportation Business Act.

Article 2 (Registration of establishment)
① Korea Ocean Business Corporation (hereinafter referred to as the "Corporation") shall register its establishment under Article 8 of the Act within two weeks from the initial payment of capital. <Amended on 2024.1.9>
② Matters to be registered under paragraph ① shall be:
1. Purpose;
2. Name;
3. Location of principal office;
4. Capital;
5. Method of capital contribution and amount paid;
6. Branch offices or local offices;
7. Name, resident registration number and address of the president;
8. Names and resident registration numbers of directors (including outside directors) and auditor;
9. Method of public notice.

Article 3 (Registration of establishment of branch offices, etc.)
Where the Corporation establishes a branch office or local office, it shall register the name, location and establishment date of that branch or local office at the location of its principal office within two weeks after establishment.

Article 4 (Registration of relocation)
① Where the Corporation relocates its principal office, it shall register the new location and relocation date at the former or new location within two weeks after relocation.
② Where the Corporation relocates a branch office or local office, it shall register the new location and relocation date at the location of its principal office within two weeks after relocation.

Article 5 (Registration of changes)
Where any registered matter under the subparagraphs of Article 2 (2) or under Article 3 changes (excluding a relocation registered under Article 4), the Corporation shall register the changed matter at the location of its principal office within two weeks after the change.

Article 6 (Registration of appointment of agents)
Where the president appoints an agent under Article 21 of the Act, the Corporation shall register the following matters at the location of its principal office within two weeks after appointment. The same shall apply when registered matters change: <Amended on 2025.1.21>
1. Name, resident registration number and address of the agent;
2. Details of any restrictions on the agent's authority.

Article 7 (Business)
① The Corporation may guarantee debts under Article 11 (1) 2-3 of the Act where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries recognizes that either of the following applies:
1. Where a sharp decline in sales and cargo volumes in the shipping and port industries causes or is expected to cause extensive harm to those industries;
2. Other cases requiring national support to respond to an urgent economic or social crisis.
② Where the Corporation intends to guarantee debts of shipping and port business operators under paragraph ①, it shall consult with the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries after a resolution by the board of directors concerning:
1. Entities whose debts are to be guaranteed;
2. Scale of debt guarantees;
3. Period of guarantees;
4. Effects of the guarantees on the Corporation's financial soundness.
③ "Duties prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 11 (1) 13 of the Act means the following: <Amended on 2024.1.9>
1. Projects involving business cooperation and exchanges with domestic and foreign policy financing institutions, research institutes, etc. related to duties under Article 11 (1) 1, 2, 2-2 through 2-4, and 3 through 9 of the Act;
2. Surveys and analyses of markets and industries relating to shipping and ports;
3. Support to improve the responsiveness of the shipping and port industries to green management under Article 2, subparagraph 5 of the Act on the Promotion of the Transition to Environment-Friendly Industrial Structures;
4. Support to enhance responsiveness of those industries to international environmental regulations adopted by international organizations, conventions and foreign governments;
5. Establishment and operation of information systems to enhance efficiency of the shipping and port industries and connected logistics systems, and support for use of those systems by shipping and port business operators.

Article 7-2 (Joint use of administrative information)
Where necessary for duties under Article 11 (1) 1, 2, 2-2 through 2-4, and 3 through 5 of the Act, the Corporation may verify administrative information specified in attached Table 1 through the joint use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act: Provided, That prior consent shall be obtained from the data subject under Article 2, subparagraph 3 of the Personal Information Protection Act when verifying administrative information containing personal information (excluding administrative information under Article 49 (2) 3 of the Enforcement Decree of the Electronic Government Act).

Article 8 (Capitalization of profit reserves, etc.)
① Before undergoing relevant procedures, including board or shareholders' meeting resolutions, to transfer profit reserves or reserves for the performance of guarantees to capital under Article 12 (3) of the Act, the Corporation shall consult with the Minister of Finance and Economy. <Amended on 2025.12.30>
② Upon transferring profit reserves or reserves for the performance of guarantees to capital under paragraph ①, the Corporation shall immediately report that fact to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries.

Article 9 (Issuance of bonds)
① Where the Corporation intends to issue bonds under Article 14 (1) of the Act, it shall establish a bond issuance plan for the relevant year including the following and obtain a resolution by the board of directors:
1. Purpose of issuing bonds;
2. Method of issuance;
3. Total amount of bonds to be issued;
4. Face value by bond denomination;
5. Interest rate of bonds;
6. Method and deadline for redemption;
7. Method and deadline for payment of interest;
8. Issue price or minimum issue price.
② The Corporation shall obtain approval from the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries for the bond issuance plan resolved by the board of directors under paragraph ① within two months from the date its budget bill is finalized.
③ Where the Corporation intends to amend a bond issuance plan approved under paragraph ②, it shall obtain a resolution by the board of directors and approval from the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries no later than ten days before the bond issue date.

Article 10 (Form of bonds)
Bonds issued by the Corporation under Article 14 (1) of the Act shall be bearer bonds: Provided, That registered bonds may be issued at the request of subscribers or holders.

Article 11 (Methods for issuing bonds)
Where the Corporation issues bonds under Article 14 (1) of the Act, it shall do so by public subscription, full underwriting or sale.

Article 12 (Subscription for bonds)
① Where the president of the Corporation intends to issue bonds by public subscription, the president shall prepare and issue a bond subscription form stating:
1. Name of the Corporation;
2. Matters under Article 9 (1) 3 through 8;
3. Total amount of outstanding bonds, if any;
4. Name and address of any company entrusted with soliciting bond subscriptions.
② A person seeking to subscribe for the Corporation's bonds shall complete, sign and seal two copies of the bond subscription form under paragraph ①, specifying the number of bonds, subscription price (or bidding price if bonds are issued at a minimum price) and the subscriber's address, and submit them.

Article 13 (Full underwriting)
Article 12 shall not apply where a specified underwriter subscribes for the entire amount of bonds under an agreement with the Corporation. Article 12 shall likewise not apply to the part of bonds subscribed for by a company entrusted with soliciting subscriptions.

Article 14 (Total amount of bonds issued)
Where the Corporation issues bonds under Article 14 (1) of the Act, it may indicate on bond subscription forms that bonds will be issued even if the total subscribed amount is less than the stated total issue amount. In such cases, the actual subscribed amount shall be the total amount of bonds issued.

Article 15 (Issue of bonds by sale)
Where the Corporation issues bonds by sale, it shall publicly announce the sales period and the matters under Article 12 (1) 1 and 2. In such cases, the president of the Corporation shall not prepare bond subscription forms.

Article 16 (Payment of subscription prices of bonds)
① Upon completion of solicitation of bond subscriptions, the Corporation shall require subscribers to pay the full subscription prices without delay.
② Where the Corporation has entrusted solicitation of bond subscriptions, the entrusted company may take the measures under paragraph ① for the Corporation in its own name and may prepare and issue bond subscription forms notwithstanding Article 12 (1).
③ Where the Corporation intends to issue bonds by public subscription, it shall not issue the bonds until the full amount corresponding to the total issue amount has been paid.

Article 17 (Matters to be stated on bonds)
The president shall state the following matters on bonds issued by the Corporation and sign and seal them: Provided, That where bonds are issued by sale, the matters under Article 9 (1) 3 shall not be stated on the bonds:
1. Name of the Corporation;
2. Matters under Article 9 (1) 3 through 7;
3. Bond number;
4. Date of issue.

Article 18 (Bond register)
① The Corporation shall keep at its principal office a bond register recording:
1. Number and serial numbers of bonds by denomination;
2. Date of issue;
3. Matters under Article 9 (1) 3 through 7;
4. Name and address of any company entrusted with soliciting bond subscriptions.
② For registered bonds, the Corporation shall additionally record the following in the bond register:
1. Name and address of the bondholder;
2. Date of acquisition of the bonds.
③ A bond owner or holder may request inspection of the bond register at any time during the Corporation's business hours.

Article 19 (Scope of public organizations)
"Public organizations prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 18 (1) of the Act means:
1. Public institutions under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions;
2. Local public corporations under Article 49 of the Local Public Enterprises Act and local public authorities under Article 76 of the same Act.

Article 20 (Supervision)
① The Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may supervise the Corporation and issue necessary orders concerning the following to ensure sound management under Article 19 (2) of the Act:
1. Budgets and settlement of accounts;
2. Establishment and amendment of business plans;
3. Management of surplus funds.
② Following consultation with the Financial Services Commission, the Minister may determine detailed matters necessary for supervision under paragraph ①, including management guidance standards. Such standards shall include:
1. Capital adequacy;
2. Asset soundness;
3. Liquidity;
4. Other matters deemed necessary to ensure sound management.

Article 21 (Credit exposure limits of the Corporation)
① Under Article 19 (2) of the Act, the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall supervise the Corporation to ensure that it does not extend credit exceeding 25 percent of its total equity to any single individual, corporation or person belonging to the same business group (meaning a business group under Article 2, subparagraph 11 of the Monopoly Regulation and Fair Trade Act; hereinafter the same shall apply). "Extension of credit" means lending money, securities or other economically valuable property, guaranteeing the performance of debts, or purchasing securities with a financing support purpose; the same shall apply hereinafter. This restriction shall not apply in any of the following cases: <Amended on 2024.1.9>
1. Where further credit is extended to a company undergoing rehabilitation proceedings under the Debtor Rehabilitation and Bankruptcy Act or jointly pursuing normalization of business management with the Corporation or financial institutions for corporate restructuring, etc.;
2. Where additional credit is extended to a person acquiring a company under subparagraph 1 as stipulated in the acquisition agreement;
3. Where the exposure limit in the main sentence of this paragraph is exceeded even though no further credit was extended under subparagraph 1 or 2, due to:
(a) An increase in the Korean won equivalent following changes in exchange rates;
(b) A decrease in the Corporation's total equity;
(c) Changes in the composition of the same business group;
(d) Merger of or transfer or acquisition of business between companies receiving credit;
(e) Other unavoidable reasons, including sudden changes in economic conditions, recognized by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries;
4. Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries recognizes that credit is necessary to respond to a crisis in the shipping industry or implement government policy, following a resolution by the board of directors.
② Credit subject to limits under paragraph ① shall include: <Amended on 2024.1.9>
1. Investment in assets relating to shipping and port businesses under Article 11 (1) 1 of the Act;
2. Debt guarantees concerning funds borrowed by shipping and port business operators under Article 11 (1) 2, 2-2 and 2-3 of the Act;
3. Purchase of bonds and shares related to shipping and port businesses under Article 11 (1) 3 of the Act;
4. Other transactions that may cause losses to the Corporation if the counterparty defaults;
5. Transactions not directly falling under subparagraphs 1 through 4 but substantially having the same effect.

Article 22 (Examination of financial soundness of the Corporation)
① Where the Financial Services Commission conducts an examination necessary to maintain the Corporation's financial soundness under Article 19 (3) of the Act, it may establish examination criteria and notify the Corporation in advance.
② Where necessary for an examination under paragraph ①, the Financial Services Commission may request the Governor of the Financial Supervisory Service to dispatch employees under the Governor's jurisdiction.
③ A person conducting an examination necessary for the Corporation's financial soundness under Article 19 (3) of the Act shall carry identification indicating his or her authority and present it to persons concerned.

Article 23 (Criteria for imposing administrative fines)
Criteria for imposing administrative fines under Article 24 (1) of the Act shall be as specified in the attached Table.

ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 29009, 2018.6.26>

Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on July 1, 2018.

Article 2 (Amendments to other statutes)
① Part of the Enforcement Decree of the Foreign Exchange Transactions Act shall be amended as follows:
Subparagraph 7 shall be newly inserted in Article 7 as follows:
7. Korea Ocean Business Corporation under the Korea Ocean Business Corporation Act.
In Article 13 (2) 1, "means the Minister of the Interior and Safety" shall be replaced with "means the Minister of the Interior and Safety, and, for Korea Ocean Business Corporation under the Korea Ocean Business Corporation Act, the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries".
In Article 14, subparagraph 4 (p), "the Community Credit Cooperatives Act and the Specialized Credit Finance Business Act" shall be replaced with "the Community Credit Cooperatives Act, the Specialized Credit Finance Business Act and the Korea Ocean Business Corporation Act".
② Part of the Enforcement Decree of the State Property Act shall be amended as follows:
Subparagraph 28 shall be newly inserted in attached Table 1 as follows:
28. Korea Ocean Business Corporation under the Korea Ocean Business Corporation Act.

